g14643.t1	eggNOG-mapper	CDS	15	271	355.0	+	.	ID=g14643.t1;em_target=3694.POPTR_0001s36580.1;em_score=355.0;em_evalue=9.95e-119;em_tcov=71.6;em_searcher=diamond;em_OGs=COG0476@1|root,KOG2017@2759|Eukaryota,37N13@33090|Viridiplantae,3GF64@35493|Streptophyta,4JDBZ@91835|fabids;em_COG_cat=H;em_desc=Plays a central role in 2-thiolation of mcm(5)S(2)U at tRNA wobble positions of cytosolic tRNA(Lys), tRNA(Glu) and tRNA(Gln). Also essential during biosynthesis of the molybdenum cofactor. Acts by mediating the C-terminal thiocarboxylation of sulfur carriers URM1 and MOCS2A. Its N-terminus first activates URM1 and MOCS2A as acyl-adenylates (-COAMP), then the persulfide sulfur on the catalytic cysteine is transferred to URM1 and MOCS2A to form thiocarboxylation (-COSH) of their C-terminus. The reaction probably involves hydrogen sulfide that is generated from the persulfide intermediate and that acts as nucleophile towards URM1 and MOCS2A. Subsequently, a transient disulfide bond is formed. Does not use thiosulfate as sulfur donor;em_max_annot_lvl=35493|Streptophyta;em_EC=2.7.7.80,2.8.1.11;em_KEGG_ko=ko:K11996;em_KEGG_Pathway=ko04122,map04122;em_KEGG_Reaction=R07459,R07461;em_KEGG_rclass=RC00043;em_BRITE=ko00000,ko00001,ko01000,ko03016,ko04121;em_PFAMs=Rhodanese,ThiF;em_Preferred_name=CNX5;em_GOs=GO:0003674,GO:0003824,GO:0005575,GO:0005622,GO:0005623,GO:0005737,GO:0008265,GO:0016740,GO:0016782,GO:0016783,GO:0044424,GO:0044464
g14643.t2	eggNOG-mapper	CDS	7	219	289.0	+	.	ID=g14643.t2;em_target=29760.VIT_19s0090g01020.t01;em_score=289.0;em_evalue=1.3e-93;em_tcov=61.7;em_searcher=diamond;em_OGs=COG0476@1|root,KOG2017@2759|Eukaryota,37N13@33090|Viridiplantae,3GF64@35493|Streptophyta;em_COG_cat=H;em_desc=Plays a central role in 2-thiolation of mcm(5)S(2)U at tRNA wobble positions of cytosolic tRNA(Lys), tRNA(Glu) and tRNA(Gln). Also essential during biosynthesis of the molybdenum cofactor. Acts by mediating the C-terminal thiocarboxylation of sulfur carriers URM1 and MOCS2A. Its N-terminus first activates URM1 and MOCS2A as acyl-adenylates (-COAMP), then the persulfide sulfur on the catalytic cysteine is transferred to URM1 and MOCS2A to form thiocarboxylation (-COSH) of their C-terminus. The reaction probably involves hydrogen sulfide that is generated from the persulfide intermediate and that acts as nucleophile towards URM1 and MOCS2A. Subsequently, a transient disulfide bond is formed. Does not use thiosulfate as sulfur donor;em_max_annot_lvl=35493|Streptophyta;em_EC=2.7.7.80,2.8.1.11;em_KEGG_ko=ko:K11996;em_KEGG_Pathway=ko04122,map04122;em_KEGG_Reaction=R07459,R07461;em_KEGG_rclass=RC00043;em_BRITE=ko00000,ko00001,ko01000,ko03016,ko04121;em_PFAMs=Rhodanese,ThiF;em_Preferred_name=CNX5;em_GOs=GO:0003674,GO:0003824,GO:0005575,GO:0005622,GO:0005623,GO:0005737,GO:0008265,GO:0016740,GO:0016782,GO:0016783,GO:0044424,GO:0044464
